[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_tumo4")
dialogue_id = "debate_inquisition"
record_title = "Debate Speech: The Holy Magistrates"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: Let us look, today, at the fate of the shard that held our very first shrine in the New World.
historian: Centuries ago, the priests there decided to question the villagers about a broken fence.
historian: I suppose people were impressed by how quickly they found the culprit, and asked them to look into other crimes.
historian: Regardless of how exactly the events escalated, their outcomes are now plain to see.
historian: Priests patrolling the streets, enforcing the holy duty of confession on anyone they meet, and exacting punishment in their holy tribunals.
historian: When you give a priest a judge's authority, you create a very dangerous kind of justice.
historian: A judge knows they are just enforcing a rule.
historian: A holy magistrate believes that they are rooting out absolute evil.
historian: There is no limit to the cruelty a person can justify when they are convinced that they are enacting a divine plan.
historian: The Scribe believes that uniting us under a single religious mandate will bring universal harmony.
historian: But this shard's story is a lesson to us all about what happens when faith becomes the law."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
